 !!! important
     The tasks are executed in order. In case one of the tasks raises
-    an exception, the following tasks will not get the opportunity to be executed.
+    an exception, the following tasks will not get the opportunity to be executed
+    by default.
+
+Set `continue_on_error=True` to execute all tasks sequentially even when a task
+raises an `Exception`. After all tasks have run, the first exception is re-raised
+with its original callback traceback. Cancellation and other `BaseException`
+failures always propagate immediately and stop the remaining tasks, even if an
+earlier task raised an ordinary exception. The `continue_on_error` option is
+keyword-only and must be a boolean; other values raise `ValueError` at construction.
